-- title:
--   The annealing numerator is fixed pointwise by projection
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$ and let $o_1,o_2$ be arbitrary Boolean functions on subset queries of $\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$. On the subsets $S$ of the paired ground $\{0,\ldots,n-1\}\times\{0,1\}$, let $\kappa(S)$ be the program's classifier, whose labels are transversal, defect $(i,k)$, and invalid. A transversal contains one member of every pair; a defect has one empty pair $i$ and one full pair $k$. For $X=\{i:(i,0)\in S\}$ and $Y=\{i:(i,1)\in S\}$, write $g_a(A)$ for the size returned by the greedy scan of $A$ using oracle $o_a$: labels are considered in increasing order and inserted precisely when the oracle accepts the enlarged set. Set $R(S)=\max(g_1(X)+|Y|+g_2(E\setminus Y)-r,0)$, where $E=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, and $d(S)=\max(n-R(S),0)$. Let $\rho\in\mathbb Q$ be arbitrary and let $\pi$ be any probability law on the finite space of paired subsets. Define $$H_\rho(S)=\begin{cases}\rho^{d(S)},&\kappa(S)=\mathrm{transversal},\\0,&\text{otherwise},\end{cases}$$ with rational values viewed as real numbers. For a finite probability law $\pi$, the observable projection $P_\pi H$ keeps $H$ on transversals, replaces it on each defect class by its $\pi$-weighted mean, and is zero on invalid states. A class of zero mass has mean zero. Then $$P_\pi H_\rho=H_\rho.$$
